      "sourceHash": "f8193e1972a5e2fbcf27977336d196f53dde9be25094af64f3fcf345e48cbf71",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.37,
          "end": 4.52,
          "en": "So that's how we can use computed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.52,
          "end": 6.68,
          "en": "Let me come back to those inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.68,
          "end": 10.62,
          "en": "I mentioned that event listening works just as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.62,
          "end": 13.64,
          "en": "You can call those methods as you need to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.64,
          "end": 17.41,
          "en": "You can forward the default event argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.41,
          "end": 19.79,
          "en": "It's forwarded automatically if you just point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.79,
          "end": 22.891,
          "en": "at the method, and you can forward any other arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.891,
          "end": 25.163,
          "en": "your methods might need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.25,
          "end": 29.5,
          "en": "But you can also use our core vue features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.5,
          "end": 31.04,
          "en": "with the composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.04,
          "end": 35.47,
          "en": "For example, V-model to add two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.47,
          "end": 37.99,
          "en": "in case you want it this year.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.99,
          "end": 41.76,
          "en": "So instead of manually listening to the input event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.76,
          "end": 43.96,
          "en": "and calling our functions here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.96,
          "end": 45.91,
          "en": "Which of course were extended is fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.91,
          "end": 50.38,
          "en": "but instead of just doing that, you can also use V-model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.38,
          "end": 54.58,
          "en": "And here's the cool thing, V-model also accepts refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.58,
          "end": 56.47,
          "en": "and reactive values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.47,
          "end": 58.91,
          "en": "So here I can just bind first name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.91,
          "end": 61.43,
          "en": "and here I just bind that last name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.43,
          "end": 65.95,
          "en": "and vue will automatically detect that these are refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.95,
          "end": 68.77,
          "en": "And it will update the value properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.77,
          "end": 71.273,
          "en": "whenever you type into those fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.24,
          "end": 76.73,
          "en": "So you don't bind dot value, instead, as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.73,
          "end": 79.42,
          "en": "in the template, when working with a ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.42,
          "end": 83.24,
          "en": "you'll always just use the ref like this without drilling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.24,
          "end": 84.8,
          "en": "into the value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.8,
          "end": 87.743,
          "en": "Vue will do this for you behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.16,
          "end": 90.93,
          "en": "So with that we're binding first name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.93,
          "end": 93.58,
          "en": "and last name here, but if we save that, we'll see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.58,
          "end": 95.16,
          "en": "that it won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.16,
          "end": 97.2,
          "en": "If I reload, I'm getting a warning already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.2,
          "end": 100.9,
          "en": "And if I type here, we see no update on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.9,
          "end": 103.35,
          "en": "And the warning is that property last name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.35,
          "end": 107.17,
          "en": "was accessed during render but it's not defined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.17,
          "end": 108.72999999999999,
          "en": "Wait what?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.72999999999999,
          "end": 110.78,
          "en": "It is defined here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.78,
          "end": 115.122,
          "en": "Well, it's defined in setup, and we're using it in template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.122,
          "end": 117.44,
          "en": "but one thing is missing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.44,
          "end": 119.8,
          "en": "We're not exposing it to the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.8,
          "end": 124.236,
          "en": "Whatever you wanna use in a template needs to be part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.236,
          "end": 127.61,
          "en": "of that object, you return at the end of setup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.61,
          "end": 131.203,
          "en": "And here, we're not returning first and last name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.06,
          "end": 136.12,
          "en": "We are returning our old update functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.12,
          "end": 138.26,
          "en": "but we're actually not using those anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.26,
          "end": 140.24,
          "en": "so we can't even delete them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.24,
          "end": 143.82,
          "en": "Instead, we should now expose first name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.82,
          "end": 146.16,
          "en": "and point and our first name or ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.16,
          "end": 149.47,
          "en": "Or use the shorthand, if we use the same key name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.47,
          "end": 151.63,
          "en": "as we have for the variable name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.63,
          "end": 153.653,
          "en": "and expose last name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.8,
          "end": 158.51,
          "en": "So we need to expose those two ref's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.51,
          "end": 160.19,
          "en": "under any names of our choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.19,
          "end": 162.55,
          "en": "for example, under the same names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.55,
          "end": 164.423,
          "en": "so that we can access them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.95,
          "end": 168.87,
          "en": "And now with that, if we save this and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.87,
          "end": 170.43,
          "en": "the warning is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.43,
          "end": 175.24,
          "en": "And now you'll see two-way binding works just as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.24,
          "end": 176.483,
          "en": "with refs here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
